# Where the ApexPrep backend is reachable from the browser.
#
# This is the only environment variable the frontend has, and it is deliberately the only place a backend URL
# appears: `src/lib/http.ts` reads it once and every request is built from there, so no component contains a
# host name. Anything Vite exposes to the browser must be prefixed `VITE_`, which is also why no secret belongs
# in this file — a VITE_ variable is compiled into the bundle and is public. API keys (Gemini, Anthropic),
# database URLs and JWT secrets live in the backend's own .env and never here.
#
# Must match an origin listed in the backend's CORS_ORIGINS, because the refresh-token cookie is sent with
# credentials and the browser will not attach it cross-origin otherwise.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
